{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Rameses, etc.</b> It was necessary for the verse to state the phrase <b>in the first month</b> twice, even though it could have said ״on the fifteenth day״ — and it would be understood that the verse speaks of the first month — or in this manner: ״and they journeyed on the fifteenth of the first month.״ Perhaps it alludes to what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Shemot Rabbah 15:11), that the month of Nisan is the time when the mazal of Israel stands firm; also, the time of the fullness of success is on the fifteenth of the month. That is what it says — <b>and they journeyed</b>, etc., <b>in the first month</b>, which is the time of the establishment of their mazal; and further, for the added grandeur of the occasion on the fifteenth, which is the time of the moon's filling out. And it says <b>to the first month</b> because this condition indicates the height of success only when it is in the month of success."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:00.834283119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}